  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Whist Minnesota. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Partnership trick-taking; no trumps; pass (red) or grand (black) each hand; first to 13 wins.',
    objective: 'Be the first partnership to reach the agreed target score (typically 13). Each hand is either Grand (take 7+ tricks) or Nula (take 6 or fewer); players secretly choose by laying a red card (pass/low) or black card (grand/high).',
    gameplay: "After the deal, each player lays one card face-down (red = pass, black = grand). If any card is black, the hand is Grand and the goal is to take at least 7 tricks; the player to the right of whoever granded leads. If all four are red (Nula), the goal is to take 6 or fewer tricks; the player to the dealer's left leads. Follow suit; highest card of the led suit wins the trick (no trumps). Winner of each trick leads the next. Scoring: Nula hands score 1 point per trick under 7 for the side that chose low; Grand hands score 1 point per trick over 6 if your side granded, or 2 points per trick over 6 if the opposing side granded.",
    keyRules: [
      'No trumps; highest of led suit wins trick.',
      'Each hand: secret pass (red) or grand (black) choice; all pass = Nula (lose tricks), any grand = Grand (win tricks).',
      'First to target score (typically 13) wins the game.',
